//==================================================
// SEP VCS coverage exclusions -- AXI fields a single internal master ties.
// Format Version: 2
// ExclMode: default
//
// Scope: the cocotb VCS elaboration of sep_uvm_top, target `default`.
// Do not merge a `rom_boot` target run against this file.
//
// Each block waives request fields on a port that exactly ONE internal master
// drives, where that master's RTL assigns the field a constant and every module
// on the path passes it unchanged. The masters are the VeeR IFU, LSU and debug
// system-bus masters, the secure DMA host port, and the key manager picorv32
// CPU. The annotation names the tie and the fields that stay graded.
//   * The sep_cpu blocks cover the IFU and debug masters on the TT wrapper's
//     own nets, from the VeeR boundary through the window remaps and demuxes,
//     and the LSU master on its VeeR boundary net (lsu_axi_req_raw) before the
//     window remap.
//   * The key manager blocks cover the KM CPU address bits [1:0] and its
//     AxPROT ties, from u_key_manager_s3c_scan and its CPU through the KM
//     AXI-Lite crossbar to each KM target: the KPV, KM CSR, mailbox KM side,
//     DRBG sampler and OTP error slave, and the key CSR blocks of the AES,
//     HMAC, KMAC, OTBN and ABR wrappers.
//
// Two rules keep this file honest:
//   * A port that the SMN inbound port, the JTAG bridge or a second master can
//     reach is NOT listed. Those fields are an integrator's to drive, so a hole
//     there is a stimulus gap.
//   * A tied field that any leaf moves is NOT listed. The no_cpu TB force
//     drives the LSU path after the window remap, so no LSU net downstream of
//     that remap is listed. No listed bit toggles in either direction in the
//     merged `all` database that supplies the checksums.
//
// Checksums come from `urg -dump full_exclusions tgl` on the merged VDB.
//==================================================

CHECKSUM: "3441942924 3928759875"
ANNOTATION: "SEP-CPU-DBG-TIED: only the VeeR debug system-bus master drives this port. el2_dbg.sv:738-774 tie id 0, prot 3'b001, AW cache 4'hF, AR cache 0, len 0, burst INCR, qos 0, lock 0, wlast 1, bready 1 and rready 1; sep_cpu.sv:501-503 and :508 drive AxUSER/WUSER to SEP_SOURCE_ID and AWATOP to 0; the window remap passes them unchanged. NOT waived: addr, size and region. SEP-DMA-MASTER-TIED: only the secure DMA host port drives this path, through axi_lite_to_axi, axi_dw_upsizer and the window remap. axi_lite_to_axi.sv:39-67 sets burst FIXED and id, len, lock, qos, region, atop and user to '0; sep_dma_wrap.sv:283-284 feed cache 4'b0000, a non-modifiable transfer the upsizer passes unchanged. hw/common/axi/tlul_to_axi_lite.sv:156 zeroes axi_lite_req_o and no branch sets prot, so DMA AxPROT is a literal 0; this file does not list prot on these nets, and sep_xbar_tie_exclusions.el waives its copies in the local crossbar. NOT waived: addr, size, prot, the W data/strobe, and wlast. The upsizer drives wlast, and a run moved it. SEP-CPU-IFU-TIED: only the VeeR IFU drives this port. el2_ifu_mem_ctl.sv:1074-1082 ties AR size 3, prot 5, cache 4'hF, len 0, burst INCR, qos 0 and lock 0; :1085-1101 hold the whole AW and W channels and bready at 0 (the IFU never writes); sep_cpu.sv:493-495 drive AxUSER/WUSER to SEP_SOURCE_ID and :506 AWATOP to 0; the window remap and IFU demux pass these fields unchanged. NOT waived: AR addr, id and region, which follow the fetch address, and rready, which a run moved. LSU path NOT waived: every field of lsu_xbar_axi_req and lsu_rom_axi_req stays graded. These nets are downstream of the LSU window remap, and the no_cpu TB force on the LSU path drives them. aw.addr bit 28 stays graded on the ports after the IFU window remap: axi_window_remap (hw/ip/axi_window_remap/rtl/axi_window_remap.sv:37-53) moves a raw address of 0 to 0x1000_0000 when SEP_LOCAL_BASE_ADDR[31:0] is 0, and that CSR is software-writable (sep_cpu_ctrl.rdl:184-191)."
