ANNOTATION: "SEP-CPU-DBG-TIED: only the VeeR debug system-bus master drives this port. el2_dbg.sv:738-774 tie id 0, prot 3'b001, AW cache 4'hF, AR cache 0, len 0, burst INCR, qos 0, lock 0, wlast 1, bready 1 and rready 1; sep_cpu.sv:501-503 and :508 drive AxUSER/WUSER to SEP_SOURCE_ID and AWATOP to 0; the window remap passes them unchanged. NOT waived: addr, size and region. SEP-CPU-IFU-TIED: only the VeeR IFU drives this port. el2_ifu_mem_ctl.sv:1074-1082 ties AR size 3, prot 5, cache 4'hF, len 0, burst INCR, qos 0 and lock 0; :1085-1101 hold the whole AW and W channels and bready at 0 (the IFU never writes); sep_cpu.sv:493-495 drive AxUSER/WUSER to SEP_SOURCE_ID and :506 AWATOP to 0; the window remap and IFU demux pass these fields unchanged. NOT waived: AR addr, id and region, which follow the fetch address, and rready, which a run moved. SEP-CPU-LSU-TIED: only the VeeR LSU drives lsu_axi_req_raw, the VeeR boundary net before the LSU window remap. el2_lsu_bus_buffer.sv:881-907 tie prot 3'b001, len 0, burst INCR, qos 0, lock 0, wlast 1, bready 1 and rready 1; sep_cpu.sv:497-499 and :507 drive AxUSER/WUSER to SEP_SOURCE_ID and AWATOP to 0. NOT waived: addr, id, size[1:0], cache and region of lsu_axi_req_raw, and every field of lsu_axi_req, lsu_rom_axi_req_o and lsu_xbar_axi_req_o. Those three nets are downstream of the LSU window remap, and the no_cpu TB force on the LSU path drives them. aw.addr bit 28 stays graded on the ports after the IFU window remap: axi_window_remap (hw/ip/axi_window_remap/rtl/axi_window_remap.sv:37-53) moves a raw address of 0 to 0x1000_0000 when SEP_LOCAL_BASE_ADDR[31:0] is 0, and that CSR is software-writable (sep_cpu_ctrl.rdl:184-191)."
